chapter(4,'evs','how-things-work','How Things Work',
 ('Meera and Dhruv explore','Every day we use things like books, pencils and toys, and some of them help us work. Have you ever wondered how they work, and how they could work even better? Meera and Dhruv love finding out. On a Sunday they spin coins and cardboard spinners and watch them wobble or stand steady, and when rain falls they make paper boats and test what floats. Let us try the same experiments and find out together.'),
 [('Spin and observe',['Meera spun a coin and watched it carefully, and you can spin things too.','Objects like coins, bangles and wooden tops spin, but an eraser does not spin properly.','As a coin slows down it begins to shake and finally falls, and a good scientist writes what she observes, what she wonders and what she thinks.','Try spinning a coin, a bangle, a pencil, a piece of stone and a wooden top, and fill in what you observe and wonder.']),
  ('Making and testing spinners',['Meera asked how a top spins, so they made spinners with cardboard pieces, toothpicks and the empty tube of a ballpoint pen.','The textbook does not expect a complete scientific explanation; the aim is to play, try and give your own possible reasons.','A spinner with the toothpick at the centre looks the same from all sides, so it stays upright and spins well.','If the toothpick or the hole is away from the centre, the spinner may not spin properly, so the position matters.','A square card looks circular when it spins fast, and you can try other shapes too.','If a spinner fails, change one thing at a time, like the length of the toothpick or how it is lined up, to find what helps.']),
  ('Colours on a spinner and spinning things around us',['You can colour a spinner in different ways and see how the colours look when it spins.','Many things around us spin, such as ceiling fans and the potter\'s wheel.','A charkha, or spinning wheel, twists cotton fibre into thread, and Mahatma Gandhi used the charkha to make handmade clothes.','Spinning tops have been used in India for thousands of years, and the lattu is a popular wooden top.']),
  ('Floating and sinking',['When the rain stopped, Dhruv and Meera made paper boats and put them in the puddle, and some floated properly while others flipped over.','Take a leaf, an iron nail, an empty steel bowl, a stone, a plastic bottle with its lid on and aluminium foil, guess first, then drop them in water.','Writing F for float and S for sink, you will find that a leaf floats and an iron nail sinks.','Heavy things like iron nails sink and light things like leaves float, but this is not the whole story.','Floating or sinking cannot be decided just by whether the object is heavy or light; other factors matter too.']),
  ('Shape matters',['Take aluminium foil and see what happens when its shape changes.','When the foil is spread out, or made into a cup shape, it floats.','When the foil is pressed tightly into a ball, it sinks.','So by changing the shape we can make an object float or sink.','Press the ball tightly so that little air is trapped, because a loosely pressed ball may even float.']),
  ('Making boats',['In groups of three or four, think of how to make a boat from paper, cardboard boxes, ice-cream sticks, clay and adhesive tape.','Draw a picture first, then make your boat, and try to make it different from the boats of other groups.','Boats can be made from ice-cream sticks, coconut shells or walnut shells too.','Compare boats in a class exhibition: some are strong and hard to break, some break easily, some tip over and some keep their balance.','Think about how you can improve your boat, which is how designers work.']),
  ('Think and figure it out',['If something spins and slowly stops, like Ravi\'s spinner, you can ask why it slows down and what makes it stop.','If a figure bends to one side, you can balance it by adding weight to the other side or moving the support.','To classify objects, test them: wax, thermocol, a candle, a cork, a leaf and an ice cube usually float, while a marble, a coin and a spoon sink.','Things like a tomato, an eraser or a lemon may depend on their kind, so test them and record what you see.'])],
 [('A foil ball sinks but a foil cup floats. What does this show?',[('Both are made of the same foil with the same weight.','Weight did not change.'),('Only the shape changed.','The ball is small and compact, the cup is wide and holds air.'),('So shape can decide whether an object floats or sinks.','Floating is not only about heavy or light.')]),
  ('Your spinner wobbles and falls. What can you change?',[('Check whether the toothpick is at the centre.','A toothpick away from the centre makes it unbalanced.'),('Change the length of the toothpick or the lining of the card.','Changing one thing at a time shows what helps.'),('Try again and record what happens.','Scientists test and observe again.')])],
 ('Explain what you learnt about floating and sinking from the activities.',['A leaf floats and an iron nail sinks','Heavy or light alone cannot decide it','The shape of an object can change floating or sinking, like aluminium foil','Always guess, test and record'],['All heavy things sink and all light things float','Shape never matters','You cannot test it']),
 ['Spinners spin steadily when the toothpick is at the centre and the shape is balanced.','Things like fans, tops, charkhas and potter\'s wheels spin.','Floating or sinking is not decided only by heavy or light.','Changing the shape of aluminium foil can make it float or sink.','Guess, test, record and improve, as when making boats.'],
 [M('1',1,'Which spinner spins steadily?','The one with the toothpick at the centre',[('The one with the toothpick away from the centre','It is unbalanced'),('A spinner with no toothpick','It needs a point to spin on')],'A centre hole or toothpick looks the same from all sides.'),
  M('2',1,'What does a charkha do?','Twists cotton fibre into thread',[('Cooks food','It is a spinning wheel'),('Pumps water','It is a spinning wheel')],'Mahatma Gandhi used the charkha to make handmade clothes.'),
  M('3',1,'What is the lattu?','A popular Indian wooden top',[('A paper boat','It is a top'),('A kind of food','It is a top')],'Spinning tops have been used in India for thousands of years.'),
  M('4',1,'In the activity, what does an iron nail do in water?','Sinks',[('Floats','A leaf floats, a nail sinks'),('Spins','It sinks')],'A heavy iron nail sinks.'),
  M('5',2,'What happens when aluminium foil is pressed into a tight ball?','It sinks',[('It floats','The spread foil or cup floats'),('It melts','Water does not melt it')],'A tight ball of foil sinks.'),
  M('6',2,'Which shape of aluminium foil floats?','Spread out flat or made into a cup',[('A tight ball','That sinks'),('None of them','Spread foil and a cup float')],'A wide shape floats.'),
  M('7',2,'Can we tell if an object will float just by checking if it is heavy or light?','No, other factors also matter',[('Yes, heavy always sinks','Some heavy things float'),('Yes, light always floats','Some light things sink')],'The shape and other things matter too.'),
  M('8',2,'Why should the foil ball be pressed tightly?','So that it traps little air',[('So that it looks round','The air is the reason'),('So that it becomes heavier','The point is trapped air')],'A loose ball with air may even float.'),
  M('9',2,'What do ceiling fans and potter\'s wheels do?','Spin',[('Float','They spin'),('Sink','They spin')],'Many things around us spin.'),
  M('10',2,'If a spinner does not work, what should you do?','Change one thing at a time and try again',[('Throw it away','Testing again helps you learn'),('Change everything together','You will not know what helped')],'Scientists test and observe again.'),
  F('11',2,'A leaf floats on water.',True,'A leaf is light and floats.'),
  F('12',3,'Shape has no effect on whether an object floats.',False,'Aluminium foil floats as a cup and sinks as a ball.')],
 svgs=[('c4evs-work-float','Water tank shows aluminium foil spread and as a cup floating, as a ball sinking, with a leaf floating and a nail sinking.','The shape of an object can change whether it floats or sinks.')],
 keep=['spinner','charkha'])
